				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Architectural targets\nGemStone 4.x is the reference platform for shared Runtime and Connect contracts. GT/Pharo is the current implementation and test platform while the required GemStone release is unavailable. Preserve native object ownership, transaction and resource semantics; label native behavior unverified until tested. Motion and Physics are GT/Pharo UI frameworks currently owned by CatalystFoundation. Their standalone repos are future extraction destinations. Theme and GT presentation remain outside portable domain contracts."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-17T07:28:46.867072+11:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-17T07:28:46.867072+11:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "KD7zN4IGRWuJZeKLCvCGHA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Fit for purpose and clear language\nImplement the smallest complete solution to the current requirement. Reuse existing framework protocols before introducing classes, adapters, dispatchers or alternate execution paths. A new abstraction needs a distinct responsibility and a demonstrated need. Class, method, argument and variable names must read as clear English and express intent. Commands use verbs, queries describe values without acting, and time/size names include units. Rename within the changed boundary and update its identified callers."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-17T07:28:47.156985+11:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-17T07:28:47.156985+11:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "mRw9uj0ITp6+4IhmcwgkEQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## One owner and one supported path\nRead {{gtPage:Catalyst framework ownership|db=731asfxqhyhdr96k6wo9yxnzv}} before implementation. Follow the owning framework contract and inspect current implementors, senders, references and examples. Record any existing path being replaced and its callers; do not keep a parallel implementation without an identified consumer and removal condition. Platform implementations may use different mechanisms under an explicit shared contract. Approved design states what must be true; source shows what is currently true. Record a mismatch as a gap rather than silently weakening the design."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-17T07:28:47.243083+11:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-17T07:28:47.243083+11:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "bqBP254YSu2B9n2A3AWefA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Efficient use of resources\nKeep durable domain state separate from activation-local processes, locks, callbacks and UI. Name the writer, queue owner, transaction boundary and failure outcome. Use ordinary native object references where appropriate; do not introduce universal serialization, copying or repository abstractions for convenience. Keep subscriptions and retained evidence bounded. Measure allocation, traversal, idle wakeups and contention before structural optimization. Connect's socket-event SharedQueue prototype and Runtime's native durable work delivery have different lifetimes and guarantees."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-17T07:28:47.282289+11:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-17T07:28:47.282289+11:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "D6IyAbA/RX6eUYg4oT6wnQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Evidence and completion\nFor each change identify the framework/package owner, relevant contract, reuse decision, changed selectors and focused checks. Update affected documentation. Distinguish source inspection, image execution results, saved source and published revisions. Record the platform, counts and exclusions for checks; historical results are not current verification.\n\nSource edits stay in the running image. Saving source files, committing and pushing are separate user-authorized actions through the DevKit's existing GT Git or Iceberg tools. Do not discover, copy or synchronize external checkouts. A second machine's filesystem is not part of Catalyst's development contract. Source does not need to be copied to another workspace to complete an image change.\n\nBuild environments exclusively with BVC using the project's configuration and startup scripts. Use existing GT tools and checks; ask before adding scripts, dependencies, infrastructure or unsupported capabilities."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
